// A spread whose operand is itself a fresh nested list literal is built at the destination's
// element type, as the literal would be without the spread, with no other source to take a row
// from (D4871). `nested-list-widen-fresh` is the twin with an `f64[][]` source beside it.
// The proof divides, so an inner list left in the i32 rep cannot print the answer.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@VALUE@@
[...[[1, 2]], ...[[3.5]]]
// @@TYPE@@
f64[][]
// @@PROOF@@
print(v[0][1] / 4.0 + v[1][0] + v.length)
// @@WANT@@
6
// @@VALUE2@@
[...[[1, 2]]]
// @@TYPE2@@
f64[][]
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v[0][1] / 4.0)
// @@WANT2@@
0.5
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a list, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
